{'symbol': 'BAC', 'date': '2023-06-13 11:07:00', 'title': 'GEORGETOWN UNIVERSITY SURVEY FINDS 65% OF YOUNG ADULTS HIGHLIGHT PAID TIME OFF AS THE TOP BENEFIT FOR CHOOSING AN EMPLOYER', 'text': 'WASHINGTON , JUNE 13, 2023 /PRNEWSWIRE/ -- A SURVEY CONDUCTED BY GEORGETOWN UNIVERSITY, IN PARTNERSHIP WITH BANK OF AMERICA, FOUND THAT YOUNG ADULTS LOOKING TO CHANGE JOB/FIELDS CITE PAID TIME OFF (65%) AND A FLEXIBLE WORK SCHEDULE (58%) AMONG THE TOP BENEFITS IMPACTING THEIR CHOICE OF AN EMPLOYER. IN ADDITION, 73% OF YOUNG ADULTS WANT BENEFITS THAT CAN TRAVEL WITH THEM IF THEY CHANGE JOBS.'}